  "body": "### Description\n\n`TrustBonding` exposes an emergency pause, but only `claimRewards()` is guarded by `whenNotPaused`. The inherited `VotingEscrow` entry points such as `create_lock()`, `increase_amount()`, `increase_unlock_time()`, and `withdraw()` never consult `paused()`, so core escrow state transitions remain live while the contract is paused.\n\n### Impact\n\nDuring an incident, the protocol cannot actually freeze lock creation, lock modification, or withdrawals even though the pause flag is set. This weakens emergency response and allows reward-relevant state to keep changing while operators believe the bonding contract is paused.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nOverride the inherited escrow mutators in `TrustBonding` and gate the intended emergency-sensitive operations with `whenNotPaused`, or explicitly document and narrow the pause semantics if withdrawals are meant to remain available.",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Proof of Concept\n\n1. An admin calls `pause()`.\n2. A user successfully calls `create_lock()` while `paused() == true`.\n3. An already-locked user can also `withdraw()` while the pause flag remains set.\n\n```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { TrustBondingBase } from \"tests/unit/TrustBonding/TrustBondingBase.t.sol\";\n\ncontract PauseBypassPoCTest is TrustBondingBase {\n    function test_poc_pauseDoesNotBlockCreateLock() external {\n        resetPrank(users.admin);\n        protocol.trustBonding.pause();\n\n        assertTrue(protocol.trustBonding.paused(), \"pause flag should be set\");\n\n        uint256 unlockTime = block.timestamp + DEFAULT_LOCK_DURATION;\n\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.wrappedTrust.approve(address(protocol.trustBonding), initialTokens);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(initialTokens, unlockTime);\n\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.totalLocked(), initialTokens, \"lock was still created while paused\");\n    }\n\n    function test_poc_pauseDoesNotBlockWithdraw() external {\n        _createLock(users.alice, initialTokens);\n\n        resetPrank(users.admin);\n        protocol.trustBonding.pause();\n\n        assertTrue(protocol.trustBonding.paused(), \"pause flag should be set\");\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + DEFAULT_LOCK_DURATION + 1 weeks);\n\n        uint256 balanceBefore = protocol.wrappedTrust.balanceOf(users.alice);\n\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.withdraw();\n\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.totalLocked(), 0, \"withdraw succeeded while paused\");\n        assertEq(\n            protocol.wrappedTrust.balanceOf(users.alice),\n            balanceBefore + initialTokens,\n            \"withdraw returned the locked tokens while paused\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n```",
